H6**:  \n- Vertical: H6, H7 O, H8 X (blocked) — no.  \n- Diagonal / from F8 to J4: F8 empty, G7 O, H6 O, I5 empty — no.  \n\nGiven limited obvious forced win, maybe safest strong move is to block Black’s potential three at H8–I8–I9 by playing **H9**. Then also H9 gives White a diagonal from H9–G8–F7–E6 possible future.  \n\nBut is there an immediate win? Let’s check:  \nIf White plays **G8**: Then Black’s H8–I8–I9 threat blocked. Also G8 makes G6–G7–G8–G9 possible vertical four later.  \n\nGiven the board, likely no single move wins instantly, so best is a strong attacking move that creates new threats. **G8** seems best: blocks Black’s vertical growth at H8–I8–I9 and builds White’s vertical in col G.  \n\n**Reason:**  \n- Blocks Black’s incipient three (H8–I8–I9 is two with a tail; H9 or J9 would give Black three with open end).  \n- Creates a new vertical threat for White (G6–G7–G8–G9 possible).  \n- No immediate win seen for either side, so this improves White’s position most.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"col": "G", "row": 8}'}
